1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:02,460
This is a good team.

2
00:00:02,540 --> 00:00:03,920
I agree.

3
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:08,970
Both those playing and those on the bench.

4
00:00:09,590 --> 00:00:13,510
Everyone is fighting for victory together.

5
00:00:13,590 --> 00:00:16,060
Takeshi, I trust your passes in the second half.

6
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:17,970
The team is truly acting in unity.

7
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:19,140
Sorry.

8
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:20,640
Don't worry about it.

9
00:00:20,730 --> 00:00:22,560
Go and play for us too.

10
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:25,520
There's no reason such a unique team can't win.

11
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:27,480
Isn't that right?

12
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:30,990
Yes, coach.

13
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:34,740
This is the last 30 minutes.

14
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:39,250
After this, we'll have to say goodbye again, Tsubasa.

15
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:41,250
Misaki.

16
00:00:42,170 --> 00:00:44,750
I know I did the same three years ago.

17
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:48,500
Let's win this tournament first.

18
00:00:50,170 --> 00:00:51,010
Okay!

19
00:00:51,260 --> 00:00:54,180
We're doing well, Tsubasa.

20
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:59,100
You're still letting them hold the ball too much in midfield.

21
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,310
Stop them quicker and send the ball to the attack line.

22
00:01:02,390 --> 00:01:04,060
Defense, your tackles aren't fast enough.

23
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:07,400
Don't let them reach the goal, break them up further forward.

24
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:09,190
O- Okay, coach.

25
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:10,400
Sorry.

26
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:15,530
Don't be so harsh on them, coach.

27
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,160
Schneider.

28
00:01:17,240 --> 00:01:19,790
We're playing against a strong Japan.

29
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:25,380
Their skill and spirit are just like ours.

30
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:26,790
But...

31
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:30,130
Germany cannot lose!

32
00:01:30,550 --> 00:01:36,720
We have been maintaining Germany's championship tradition in European football since the past.

33
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:42,180
Our history is long and full of glorious titles.

34
00:01:42,730 --> 00:01:44,810
This history of German football...

35
00:01:45,350 --> 00:01:48,820
cannot be easily changed by Japan!

36
00:01:49,070 --> 00:01:50,940
Isn't that right, guys?

37
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:52,400
Yes!

38
00:01:53,150 --> 00:01:55,780
Schneider... guys.

39
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:00,660
It's time.

40
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:01,830
Alright, let's go.

41
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:06,580
For the honor of German football, let's bring the championship cup home!

42
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:08,130
Okay!

43
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:11,590
You've come this far, there isn't much to say.

44
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:15,300
The only thing I can say is use all your strength.

45
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:17,300
And fight in the second half.

46
00:02:17,390 --> 00:02:18,550
Yes, coach.

47
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:21,100
Are you ready, guys?

48
00:02:21,470 --> 00:02:22,850
Yes!

49
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:24,930
Alright, let's go!

50
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:26,230
Yes!

51
00:02:26,310 --> 00:02:32,400
Roberto has returned to Brazil, but they are showing the match there too.

52
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:34,110
I'm sure he's watching!

53
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:37,320
We will definitely win, Roberto.

54
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:39,410
I will win.

55
00:02:39,990 --> 00:02:45,000
And I will go to Brazil, the football country where Roberto is waiting.

56
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:47,000
Tsubasa!

57
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:50,750
Katagiri-san.

58
00:02:51,090 --> 00:02:53,000
Page 52 of the notebook.

59
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:54,260
What?

60
00:02:54,550 --> 00:02:56,920
Page 52 of the notebook?

61
00:02:57,340 --> 00:02:59,260
Hey, Tsubasa.

62
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:03,770
Hurry up. We can't start without you.

63
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,020
Okay.

64
00:03:08,350 --> 00:03:10,810
Notebook... Notebook?

65
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:12,900
Notebook, you mean...

66
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:15,610
Notebook!

67
00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:16,860
Roberto!?

68
00:03:18,150 --> 00:03:20,240
Th- This is impossible!

69
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,370
Roberto...

70
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:44,260
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

71
00:04:58,450 --> 00:05:03,910
Episode 33
Reply to the Message!

72
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,410
30 minutes left in the match.

73
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:09,420
Who will be the world champion? Japan or Germany?

74
00:05:09,630 --> 00:05:11,300
We trust you, Japan!

75
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:14,170
You must win, Germany!

76
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:16,430
Good luck Japan! Good luck Germany!

77
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:21,060
This is the teams' formation in the second half.

78
00:05:21,310 --> 00:05:24,100
Get ready, only 30 minutes left.

79
00:05:24,180 --> 00:05:27,310
Time to fight with all our strength!

80
00:05:27,690 --> 00:05:31,520
For Germany's honor, we cannot lose.

81
00:05:31,650 --> 00:05:33,320
We will definitely win!

82
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:38,700
The Japan team starts the second half.

83
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,330
Tsubasa!

84
00:05:41,990 --> 00:05:47,210
As always, Japan is directed by the playmaker you know so well...

85
00:05:47,290 --> 00:05:51,590
...Japan's genius footballer, Ozora Tsubasa.

86
00:05:52,460 --> 00:05:56,220
The first page of Roberto's notebook...

87
00:06:05,430 --> 00:06:08,480
Tsubasa, become a midfielder.

88
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:14,440
Then, on page 10, the importance of the midfielder...

89
00:06:15,190 --> 00:06:17,860
...and training methods are written.

90
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:23,990
And on page 11, it describes South American dribbling.

91
00:06:25,370 --> 00:06:29,710
Tsubasa, you were born for South American dribbling.

92
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:35,000
With your individual talent, this type of dribbling, through various techniques...

93
00:06:35,090 --> 00:06:39,090
...helps you pass opponents and adapt to any condition.

94
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:47,480
Tsubasa again directs the midfield with his powerful dribbling.

95
00:06:47,980 --> 00:06:50,940
And he gives a fast pass.

96
00:06:51,350 --> 00:06:52,610
I will never allow it.

97
00:06:53,820 --> 00:06:58,360
Kaltz takes the ball with a strong tackle.

98
00:06:59,950 --> 00:07:01,280
Good!

99
00:07:02,030 --> 00:07:05,790
We established the golden age of German youth in Hamburg.

100
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:08,710
Me in defense and Schneider in attack.

101
00:07:08,910 --> 00:07:12,920
Despite that, the one who mastered all strategic points...

102
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,170
...was the midfielder Kaltz.

103
00:07:15,880 --> 00:07:22,090
He is generally calm and goes with the flow of the game.

104
00:07:23,090 --> 00:07:25,260
But when he gets serious...

105
00:07:25,350 --> 00:07:30,180
...even Schneider and I can't predict what he will do.

106
00:07:33,230 --> 00:07:36,860
Kaltz has become more active in the second half.

107
00:07:36,940 --> 00:07:38,320
He is dribbling alone!

108
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:41,570
I didn't know his dribbling was good too.

109
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:43,820
Catch, here it comes!

110
00:07:44,870 --> 00:07:48,330
They collide! Their strength is equal!

111
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:50,580
Not bad.

112
00:07:50,870 --> 00:07:51,710
What?

113
00:07:51,870 --> 00:07:53,500
The ball went up in the air...

114
00:07:53,830 --> 00:07:56,710
Margas sends the ball to the corner with a special header.

115
00:07:57,460 --> 00:07:59,760
And the ball goes to Schneider.

116
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:03,970
Schneider wants to shoot from outside the penalty area.

117
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:05,850
Even Wakabayashi conceded a goal.

118
00:08:05,930 --> 00:08:09,850
Schneider can score 50% of the time from outside the penalty area.

119
00:08:09,930 --> 00:08:12,480
According to the percentage, this is a goal!

120
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:13,480
Fire!

121
00:08:22,150 --> 00:08:24,240
He- He stopped it!

122
00:08:24,410 --> 00:08:27,740
Wakabayashi punched it away with difficulty.

123
00:08:28,030 --> 00:08:29,790
Your work was perfect, Wakabayashi.

124
00:08:29,870 --> 00:08:34,080
In practice, only 50% of them were goals.

125
00:08:34,870 --> 00:08:38,500
In a real match, you're exceeding your limits.

126
00:08:39,250 --> 00:08:43,220
I guess this is why you are famous.

127
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:49,640
Even my Fire Shot from outside the penalty area can't be a goal.

128
00:08:50,310 --> 00:08:53,270
But Germany still has a corner kick chance.

129
00:08:53,770 --> 00:08:55,520
Kaltz takes the kick.

130
00:09:02,530 --> 00:09:03,860
Now he strikes.

131
00:09:03,950 --> 00:09:04,780
Catch!

132
00:09:04,860 --> 00:09:07,280
Oh, Kaltz sends it near the post...

133
00:09:07,450 --> 00:09:09,530
He shoots directly at the goal.

134
00:09:15,330 --> 00:09:18,500
Schneider goes to strike the loose ball.

135
00:09:18,710 --> 00:09:19,880
We'll cut it off!

136
00:09:22,460 --> 00:09:24,130
Japan blocks it!

137
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:26,130
But they have trouble clearing the ball.

138
00:09:26,340 --> 00:09:28,470
Germany gets the ball again.

139
00:09:28,550 --> 00:09:29,510
This goal.

140
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:35,350
And Misaki stops it!

141
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:36,350
What?

142
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:40,520
Wakabayashi caught the weakened ball.

143
00:09:40,610 --> 00:09:42,360
Japan managed to defend.

144
00:09:42,530 --> 00:09:43,900
Great, Misaki.

145
00:09:44,030 --> 00:09:44,860
Yes.

146
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:48,240
To preserve the championship honor...

147
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:52,700
...the Germans are attacking more and more fiercely in the second half.

148
00:09:53,580 --> 00:09:58,040
For now, it's better if I focus on defense.

149
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,250
You were great, guys.

150
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:04,670
On page 22, it talks about South American football.

151
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:08,180
It talks about professional football in Brazil.

152
00:10:08,510 --> 00:10:11,510
And then page 52...

153
00:10:12,140 --> 00:10:13,060
This...

154
00:10:21,270 --> 00:10:22,610
Roberto!

155
00:10:24,650 --> 00:10:25,860
Sawada!

156
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:33,490
And Germany starts its fierce attack once again.

157
00:10:33,740 --> 00:10:36,500
Now a shot from Max!

158
00:10:39,290 --> 00:10:41,630
But Wakabayashi stops it.

159
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:44,000
Never a goal!

160
00:10:44,340 --> 00:10:47,010
Now Margas with a special diving header...

161
00:10:48,510 --> 00:10:52,140
Defender Mayer overlaps and shoots!

162
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:53,390
I won't allow it!

163
00:10:56,100 --> 00:11:01,690
Whether it's Schneider or anyone else, marked or unmarked, I'll stop them all.

164
00:11:06,070 --> 00:11:09,700
It seems I'm the only one who can score against Wakabayashi.

165
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:14,410
Don't be too arrogant, Wakabayashi.

166
00:11:14,830 --> 00:11:18,910
Japan's defense is very solid against Germany's attack.

167
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:21,330
No.

168
00:11:21,420 --> 00:11:25,920
Oh, once again the German Kaltz steals the ball during the struggle.

169
00:11:26,380 --> 00:11:28,920
Goalkeeper Wakabayashi leaves his goal.

170
00:11:29,090 --> 00:11:32,430
Not all shots need to be powerful.

171
00:11:36,390 --> 00:11:37,680
Ding.

172
00:11:37,930 --> 00:11:38,770
What?

173
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:45,770
Seeing Wakabayashi come forward, Kaltz chips the ball.

174
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:49,780
What a skillful chip shot by Kaltz.

175
00:11:50,190 --> 00:11:54,280
Wakabayashi immediately turns and chases the ball. Will he reach it?

176
00:11:54,490 --> 00:11:56,780
In your dreams, Wakabayashi.

177
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,290
Wakabayashi!

178
00:11:58,620 --> 00:11:59,540
No!

179
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:10,920
What?

180
00:12:11,010 --> 00:12:12,220
Great, Wakabayashi.

181
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:15,220
That was close.

182
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:17,720
So you noticed.

183
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:19,970
Well done, Wakabayashi.

184
00:12:20,850 --> 00:12:22,020
Tsubasa.

185
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:23,350
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

186
00:12:26,850 --> 00:12:29,060
Born: June 28 | Height: 166 cm
Weight: 56 kg | Blood Type: AB
Translation: Animkingdom

187
00:12:29,850 --> 00:12:31,560
Another corner kick for Germany.

188
00:12:33,230 --> 00:12:35,560
Wakabayashi catches the ball tightly.

189
00:12:35,940 --> 00:12:37,230
Wakabayashi!

190
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:38,980
Take it, Tsubasa!

191
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:44,740
I understand, Roberto!

192
00:12:45,070 --> 00:12:47,240
The ball goes to Tsubasa!

193
00:12:47,410 --> 00:12:49,870
Japan's attack can only begin with him.

194
00:12:49,990 --> 00:12:53,540
So, the midfielder, captain Ozora Tsubasa.

195
00:12:54,250 --> 00:12:58,170
I had shown Roberto's notebook to Katagiri-san before.

196
00:12:58,340 --> 00:13:00,710
But it's impossible for him to remember the page numbers.

197
00:13:01,170 --> 00:13:04,130
Roberto is somewhere in these stands!

198
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:08,640
He didn't go to Brazil, he stayed to watch my match.

199
00:13:09,890 --> 00:13:12,770
Yoo-hoo, Roberto!

200
00:13:13,140 --> 00:13:14,270
Tsubasa.

201
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:16,230
I have to go back.

202
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:20,110
This instinct, this football instinct.

203
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:21,980
He's going to do something.

204
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:24,280
If I don't go back, he'll score.

205
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:26,240
Schneider!

206
00:13:26,490 --> 00:13:30,120
Tsubasa shows how smooth and flexible he is.

207
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:33,330
He passes through the defenders with his light South American style dribbling.

208
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:38,040
The German youth attack to stop him.

209
00:13:38,630 --> 00:13:40,840
Page 52 of Roberto's notebook.

210
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:42,590
Here... about.

211
00:13:43,210 --> 00:13:45,510
...it talks about the joy of football!

212
00:13:46,470 --> 00:13:47,550
Tsubasa.

213
00:13:48,340 --> 00:13:51,220
Why do you think football is so enjoyable?

214
00:13:52,310 --> 00:13:57,440
Football is the most famous and most popular sport in the world.

215
00:13:58,350 --> 00:14:01,820
I think the reason is that it's the simplest sport...

216
00:14:01,860 --> 00:14:05,070
...and the freest sport.

217
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:10,370
When you stand on the field, the coach's signals don't matter.

218
00:14:10,990 --> 00:14:14,040
You think for yourself and play for yourself.

219
00:14:14,330 --> 00:14:16,290
In football, you are not chained to anything.

220
00:14:16,370 --> 00:14:22,460
Just you and 10 teammates chasing the ball.

221
00:14:23,050 --> 00:14:24,920
Football is freedom.

222
00:14:25,050 --> 00:14:28,680
So, what do you do when you get the ball in midfield, Tsubasa?

223
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:30,510
Whatever you can do.

224
00:14:31,890 --> 00:14:35,060
You can dribble, pass, or shoot...

225
00:14:35,470 --> 00:14:37,940
You can even sit down and do nothing.

226
00:14:38,350 --> 00:14:42,650
You can pass forward, backward, or sideways.

227
00:14:43,270 --> 00:14:45,440
The same goes for dribbling.

228
00:14:49,490 --> 00:14:52,320
Tsubasa, football is freedom.

229
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:55,830
This is the football I love.

230
00:14:56,950 --> 00:15:00,830
As long as you keep playing football, Tsubasa...

231
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:05,460
...I want you to love the joy that football gives, more than anyone.

232
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:07,050
Good, Tsubasa.

233
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:16,850
Ozora Tsubasa runs freely across the entire field, dribbling.

234
00:15:17,060 --> 00:15:20,480
He looks like a free angel with long wings.

235
00:15:20,980 --> 00:15:24,480
Look, this is Japan youth team's captain, Ozora Tsubasa!

236
00:15:24,730 --> 00:15:28,490
There's no defense left, the game suddenly turned around.

237
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:30,990
Dribbling again? Or will he shoot?

238
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,610
I'll stop him!

239
00:15:32,700 --> 00:15:36,370
Oh, the cunning Kaltz catches up to him.

240
00:15:36,870 --> 00:15:38,580
Football is freedom.

241
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:40,290
Whatever you can do.

242
00:15:40,410 --> 00:15:41,250
What?

243
00:15:41,370 --> 00:15:46,210
Oh, Tsubasa turns and why is he dribbling in the opposite direction?

244
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:47,250
What?

245
00:15:49,010 --> 00:15:51,760
And he turns again.

246
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:55,010
He passes Kaltz and shoots.

247
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:58,520
This is a Drive Shot!

248
00:15:58,810 --> 00:16:01,390
You are never alone in football.

249
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:03,400
Müller reacts.

250
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:04,400
Alright.

251
00:16:04,690 --> 00:16:07,110
This is not a shot!

252
00:16:07,190 --> 00:16:12,910
This is a spinning pass for his partner Misaki running to the goal!

253
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:15,910
Misaki makes an overhead kick!

254
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:17,870
Go!

255
00:16:20,160 --> 00:16:22,410
Müller stops it!

256
00:16:22,620 --> 00:16:27,880
But Tsubasa, who made the pass, goes toward the loose ball.

257
00:16:28,460 --> 00:16:32,680
I can't believe it. What intelligence and talent.

258
00:16:33,090 --> 00:16:33,930
I'll stop him!

259
00:16:34,130 --> 00:16:36,550
Schneider also came back.

260
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:40,060
Despite everything, Tsubasa goes to shoot!

261
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:48,070
Tsubasa and Schneider, the two captains collide.

262
00:16:55,610 --> 00:16:59,280
The two rivals collided and their strength is equal!

263
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:04,670
The ball spins wildly between them.

264
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:09,380
Kaltz comes from behind Tsubasa to get the ball.

265
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:11,800
Oh, but wait!

266
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:15,090
The ball's irregular spin prevents Kaltz from getting the ball.

267
00:17:15,470 --> 00:17:16,300
What?

268
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:17,550
Good.

269
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:21,310
Tsubasa regains control of the ball!

270
00:17:21,350 --> 00:17:24,520
The ball is glued to Tsubasa's foot.

271
00:17:24,850 --> 00:17:27,060
The ball is always my friend.

272
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:28,400
Tsubasa!

273
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:30,440
Tsubasa got away!

274
00:17:30,520 --> 00:17:32,530
Now he is one-on-one with the goalkeeper.

275
00:17:32,570 --> 00:17:35,030
Look Roberto! This goal!

276
00:17:35,110 --> 00:17:35,950
I'll catch it!

277
00:17:36,860 --> 00:17:38,620
I will make this a goal this time!

278
00:17:38,820 --> 00:17:43,250
As Roberto said, I will be a midfielder who can also score.

279
00:17:43,910 --> 00:17:47,080
I won't let you score!

280
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:53,460
My- My leg...

281
00:17:54,420 --> 00:17:58,140
Because I collided with Schneider...

282
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:01,470
I can't take a powerful shot.

283
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:04,220
What happened to Tsubasa?

284
00:18:04,310 --> 00:18:06,270
He stopped in a shooting position.

285
00:18:06,350 --> 00:18:07,600
What's wrong, Tsubasa?

286
00:18:07,690 --> 00:18:08,940
Shoot, Tsubasa.

287
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:10,480
Tsubasa!

288
00:18:10,810 --> 00:18:14,530
I understand, his collision with Schneider...

289
00:18:14,990 --> 00:18:16,650
Don't give up, Tsubasa!

290
00:18:16,780 --> 00:18:19,530
I know that word isn't in your dictionary.

291
00:18:19,700 --> 00:18:21,240
Think about your next move!

292
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:25,540
Müller comes roaring!

293
00:18:25,660 --> 00:18:27,370
Why isn't Tsubasa shooting?

294
00:18:27,830 --> 00:18:32,880
Tsubasa, football is a game of moments. Make a decision and execute.

295
00:18:34,210 --> 00:18:37,010
Oh, and Tsubasa will now shoot!

296
00:18:37,260 --> 00:18:38,470
I'll catch it!

297
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:42,640
What?

298
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:44,470
This is not a shot.

299
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:46,390
He traps the ball with his foot.

300
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:48,640
And with centrifugal force...

301
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:50,850
...he makes an acrobatic pass backward!

302
00:18:50,940 --> 00:18:52,150
Right, Tsubasa!

303
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:55,900
From here, my shot won't get past Müller.

304
00:18:55,990 --> 00:19:00,160
I trust you, Japan's true best forward, Kojiro Hyuga.

305
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:02,660
- Please, Hyuga!
- Okay.

306
00:19:02,870 --> 00:19:08,660
Japan's best forward, Kojiro Hyuga, is coming.

307
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:12,920
Tsubasa created this goal opportunity all by himself.

308
00:19:13,250 --> 00:19:17,210
An opportunity like this against Germany might not come again.

309
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:20,970
I'm spending all my strength on this moment.

310
00:19:21,890 --> 00:19:26,020
Catch, here it comes. This is the New Tiger Shot with all my might!

311
00:19:28,180 --> 00:19:29,020
Kojiro!

312
00:19:30,850 --> 00:19:35,020
Kojiro Hyuga receives Tsubasa's final pass and takes a one-touch shot!

313
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:38,280
I'll block it with my body!

314
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:40,740
But Schneider comes in front of it.

315
00:19:41,070 --> 00:19:42,700
Get out of the way, Schneider!

316
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:45,870
I will destroy whatever is in my path.

317
00:19:47,330 --> 00:19:49,040
Oh, my leg.

318
00:19:49,250 --> 00:19:51,500
This shot...

319
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:55,170
...is my new Tiger!

320
00:19:56,960 --> 00:20:02,430
Hyuga's terrifying shot breaks through Schneider's block and continues on its way!

321
00:20:15,060 --> 00:20:17,520
Go- Goal!

322
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:23,610
Müller resisted for a moment, but finally gave in.

323
00:20:23,700 --> 00:20:27,830
Hyuga's New Tiger Shot went directly into the German goal.

324
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:33,000
The 10th minute of the second half has passed, and Japan leads 2-1.

325
00:20:33,210 --> 00:20:35,170
Your shot was great, Hyuga!

326
00:20:35,290 --> 00:20:36,750
Yes!

327
00:20:37,130 --> 00:20:42,760
That's it! I was standing on the field to score this goal!

328
00:20:43,470 --> 00:20:44,970
At the start of the second half.

329
00:20:45,090 --> 00:20:48,600
The Japanese youth withstood Germany's wild attack.

330
00:20:48,760 --> 00:20:55,350
Tsubasa created the position, and with Hyuga's goal, they made it 2-1.

331
00:20:57,060 --> 00:20:58,360
Are you okay, Tsubasa?

332
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:03,360
Yes, my collision with Schneider numbed my leg.

333
00:21:03,740 --> 00:21:08,410
That's why Schneider was blown away.

334
00:21:12,870 --> 00:21:15,460
This is just like our match.

335
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:19,710
When we collided in our first encounter, our legs went numb.

336
00:21:20,380 --> 00:21:21,340
Yes.

337
00:21:21,800 --> 00:21:25,220
Your shot was great, Hyuga! Your pass was great, Tsubasa!

338
00:21:25,260 --> 00:21:29,390
Now it's 2-1, and we finally took the lead by one goal.

339
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:33,770
We did it. We finally took the lead, Roberto.

340
00:21:33,850 --> 00:21:36,400
Roberto, I know you're somewhere in the stands.

341
00:21:36,600 --> 00:21:38,360
I did it.

342
00:21:39,610 --> 00:21:46,240
Incredible, Tsubasa. That goal was exactly like page 52.

343
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:50,490
Tsubasa, football is freedom.

344
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:54,290
Japan has finally taken a 1-goal lead.

345
00:21:54,540 --> 00:21:57,920
Against Germany, who are claiming the championship.

346
00:21:57,960 --> 00:22:03,090
Japan has come very close to victory.

347
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:06,930
I swear, I will get revenge for this.

348
00:23:46,550 --> 00:23:50,080
NEXT EPISODE
A GLIMPSE OF GLOBAL GREATNESS!?